WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.040
Welcome to our second drink of Goodbye, Toby, part two.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.260
So much happens in this episode.

3
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.940
It's like the season four cliffhanger.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:10.600
Yes.

5
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.060
And while we did our best to cover everything,

6
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.780
some of you wrote in with story moments

7
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.300
that you wished we had covered.

8
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.480
Like Jory L wrote in to say,

9
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.040
I'm kind of sad they didn't mention the voicemail

10
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.120
Jim left Ryan.

11
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.540
It was so funny.

12
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.360
Oh my God, it is so funny.

13
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.860
Okay, so it's right after Ryan gets arrested

14
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.940
and it's a major Jim sass.

15
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.620
Well, I think we need to hear it.

16
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.980
Hey, Ryan, it's Jim.

17
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:34.900
You know what?

18
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.980
Totally disregard that last voicemail

19
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.020
because you obviously have your hands tied.

20
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.560
Good luck.

21
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:41.740
Get it?

22
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.660
He has his hands tied.

23
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.000
Right, not hands full.

24
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.220
Yeah, because he's just been cuffed.

25
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:46.600
Right.

26
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.640
Jim sass.

27
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.880
All right, I wanted to share something fun

28
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.660
that I found on disc four from season nine.

29
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.240
It's in that section called A Look Back.

30
00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.200
It's like a compilation.

31
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.160
It's a tearjerker when you watch it.

32
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.160
We've talked about it.

33
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.500
In the finale episode.

34
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.260
But there was a moment where Ed Helms

35
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.940
talks about the proposal scene

36
00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.780
between Andy and Angela.

37
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.480
Oh, that happens in this episode.

38
00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.760
That happens in this episode.

39
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.840
Again, I'm hugely pregnant.

40
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.840
They're trying to hide it.

41
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.340
But here's some of Ed's memories of that moment.

42
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.320
I think the scene where Andy proposed to Angela

43
00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:30.140
Angela was very fitting because it was so left-footed and just awkward.

44
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.540
Angela's response was not good.

45
00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.320
It really summed up the tension, the misunderstanding, the denial,

46
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.420
all these awful things that kind of underpinned their relationship.

47
00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.600
Mm-hmm.

48
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.320
All true.

49
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.560
That response was horrible.

50
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.300
Like, when you married, you're just like, okay, sure.

51
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.200
I know.

52
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.420
Well, listen, we also got a fan mail flurry for this episode.

53
00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.820
Folks, really needed me to know that the Dan Band is not in the movie The Wedding Singer.

54
00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.820
I said they were in The Wedding Singer.

55
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.620
They were, in fact, in The Hangover and Old School.

56
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.020
Thank you so much.

57
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.160
I think I was thinking of Old School.

58
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:10.860
Mm-hmm.

59
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.740
But I also just recently re-watched The Hangover,

60
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.600
and they are also in that.

61
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:17.080
Yeah.

62
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.420
Which, by the way, The Hangover is a bonkers movie.

63
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.260
Bonkers.

64
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.300
How much can happen to those group of guys?

65
00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:23.940
My God.

66
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:24.700
So much.

67
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.260
So funny.

68
00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.300
All those guys are so funny.

69
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.880
Ed is so funny in it.

70
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.160
Ed is amazing in it.

71
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:34.760
But lastly, a lot of you wrote in about how much you loved the alt-Michael-Goodbye-Toby songs

72
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:35.780
that Paul Lieberstein wrote.

73
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.460
Jenna, you had shared this with us, and we actually had Josh, my husband,

74
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.100
sing Beers in Heaven, and Jordan Duffy sing Totally Clips of the Fart.

75
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:45.640
Yes.

76
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.220
And we played those in the episode, but we never actually played the song that aired,

77
00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.540
the one that Michael sings to Toby.

78
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.880
It happens and starts and stops because there's talking heads that interrupt it,

79
00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:02.800
but a bunch of folks online have pieced it all together so you can hear it as one.

80
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:03.420
Yes.

81
00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.960
It's so crazy.

82
00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.960
I forgot how crazy this song is.

83
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.460
Here's one that was compiled by Randy M.

84
00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.180
It was early morning yesterday.

85
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.620
I was up before the dawn.

86
00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.320
I really have enjoyed my stay.

87
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.280
Toby must be moving on.

88
00:03:26.060 --> 00:04:10.200
I just started, finally, watching The Office from the beginning with my two kids.

89
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.740
Okay, we're in the middle of season three.

90
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:20.860
I cannot wait for them to see that because they love how much Michael hates Toby.

91
00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.720
My kids, of course, love Dwight.

92
00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.700
My son laughed so hard.

93
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:33.380
You know when conflict resolution, when Michael's reading off all of Dwight's complaints,

94
00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:38.180
and the thing about, like, I hit myself in the head with the phone,

95
00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.480
and Michael's like, how would that have been Jim's fault?

96
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.540
And then Jim explains the thing.

97
00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.400
Explains the coins, the weighted headset.

98
00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.900
That put my son on the floor, and that is my favorite prank.

99
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:54.700
So it's so fun to share it with them now, and I cannot wait for them to see this scene.

100
00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:59.060
I forgot how many little extra, like, quips that Steve threw in.

101
00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.060
Like, see ya!

102
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.160
Yeah, exactly.

103
00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.460
He's out of here!

104
00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.680
Like, at the end.

105
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.880
It's great.

106
00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.700
All right, everyone, here is your second drink of Goodbye, Toby, part two.

107
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.420
I'm Jenna Fisher.

108
00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.720
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

109
00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.000
We were on The Office together.

110
00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.240
And we're best friends.

111
00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.080
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

112
00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:27.800
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories

113
00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.060
that only two people who were there can tell you.

114
00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.180
We're The Office ladies.

115
00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.040
All right, everybody, we are still saying goodbye to Toby.

116
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.160
It is Goodbye, Toby, part two.

117
00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.100
It's a long goodbye, but he deserves it.

118
00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.700
He's been at the company a long time.

119
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.980
He deserves a two-parter.

120
00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.500
Michael's gonna give him a big send-off, lady.

121
00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.700
He sure is.

122
00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:57.660
Guys, it's season four, episode 19, written by Jen Salata and Paul Lieberstein, directed

123
00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.060
by Paul Feig.

124
00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.960
Here is a summary of part two of Goodbye, Toby.

125
00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:03.760
Okay.

126
00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:10.500
An extravagant goodbye party is being thrown in the parking lot for Toby.

127
00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.380
Ryan is arrested for fraud.

128
00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.380
Michael discovers big news about Jan.

129
00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:24.080
Jim plans to propose to Pam, but gets upstaged by Andy, and Phyllis discovers a secret.

130
00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.840
Does she ever?

131
00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:29.420
All right.

132
00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.600
Jumping right in.

133
00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.060
Fast fact number one.

134
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.280
I'm calling this party time.

135
00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.160
Are you gonna give me a breakdown of all the party?

136
00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:38.700
You know I am.

137
00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:43.220
We got fan questions from Abby M and Yvette M.

138
00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:47.440
How many days did it take to film Toby's goodbye party?

139
00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.860
How long did it take to set it up?

140
00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:52.100
Well, you know I went to Kentopedia.

141
00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:58.700
He said it took one full day to set it up and two days and nights to film.

142
00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.960
We filmed April 17th and 18th of 2008.

143
00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:09.140
The Ferris wheel came from a company called Awesome Events,

144
00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:14.840
and it cost us $7,500 to rent that Ferris wheel for three days.

145
00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:15.940
Dang.

146
00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:16.840
Mm-hmm.

147
00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.180
That's a pricey Ferris wheel.

148
00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.180
Here's what I remember about those party scenes, Angela.

149
00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:26.860
It was very hot during the day, and then at night it got cold.

150
00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:27.480
Yeah.

151
00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.920
I remember I had hand warmers in my pockets at night,

152
00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:35.920
and you know when you go skiing and you put those toe warmers in your ski boots?

153
00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.980
I had those in my shoes for the night shoot.

154
00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.940
Also, whenever they didn't see our feet, we had Uggs on,

155
00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:47.140
and Jenna, I have an Ugg catch later in this episode.

156
00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.920
Whose Uggs do you see?

157
00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.200
Not going to tell.

158
00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.540
Guys, you're going to have to wait for it.

159
00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.660
She's making you wait for it.

160
00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.560
Also, in between takes, do you remember our wardrobe department had these big,

161
00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.560
puffy coats, like the kind that go down to your ankles?

162
00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:10.240
Giant puffy coats, and they would bring them out to us so that we could put them on

163
00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.500
in between takes outside when we were cold.

164
00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.840
And you know what?

165
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:15.700
What?

166
00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.320
I still have mine.

167
00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:18.420
You do?

168
00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.000
Oh, what a score.

169
00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:20.700
Yeah.

170
00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:26.540
And on the label, on the inside of the coat, it says Pam, written in Sharpie.

171
00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:27.560
Aww.

172
00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.440
Because that's how they knew whose coat belonged to who.

173
00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:31.240
They Sharpied it.

174
00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.600
Well, these were like giant sleeping bags.

175
00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.120
Yes.

176
00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.280
Made into jackets.

177
00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:36.940
Well described.

178
00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:38.240
Okay.

179
00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.760
Fast fact number two.

180
00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.560
I'm kind of sad.

181
00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.120
I know.

182
00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.360
This is not just goodbye, Toby.

183
00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:46.300
Nope.

184
00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.600
This is goodbye, Kentopedia.

185
00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:49.740
Yes.

186
00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.120
Kent Svornak.

187
00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.280
This was the end of his run on The Office.

188
00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.180
Yeah.

189
00:08:54.520 --> 00:09:02.680
After this, he moved on, and he became the producer and production manager for Anger Management,

190
00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.900
Dear White People, and most recently, The Conners.

191
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.560
He is an amazing, amazing production manager, you guys.

192
00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.780
We were so lucky to have him for four seasons.

193
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:19.720
And Office Ladies has been so lucky that he saved, like, everything.

194
00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.900
Talk about digital hoarder.

195
00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.980
Kentopedia is giving you a run for your money, Angela.

196
00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:27.900
Well, I think he's beat me, but I just love him.

197
00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.720
And we loved him so much.

198
00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:36.580
Jenna, in anticipation of this being his last episode, I went through and found all of these

199
00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.600
emails during this week that I traded with Kent.

200
00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:44.460
This was, like, towards the end of my pregnancy, and he and I were having to schedule a lot of

201
00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:47.960
things around my OB-GYN appointments and everything.

202
00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:53.400
And if I could share anything with you guys is the kindness and the thoughtfulness that

203
00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:58.660
this man had for every member of the cast in making the show the best it could be.

204
00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:02.060
And we were so sad to see him go.

205
00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.680
I just love this guy.

206
00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:04.920
I love him, too.

207
00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.900
And I love being in touch with him.

208
00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:10.680
And he was so great to us on The Office, and he's been so great to us on Office Ladies.

209
00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.200
We love you, Kentopedia.

210
00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.080
We love you, Kentopedia.

211
00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.720
And I'm going to share a few of our emails later in this episode.

212
00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:23.900
Angela, I want to share one of my favorite fun facts about Kent as we say goodbye to him.

213
00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:24.820
Okay, what?

214
00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:31.320
In his youth, Kent was an assistant to the creator of Golden Girls.

215
00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:32.740
Her name is Susan Harris.

216
00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:40.880
And she loved Kent's last name so much that when she wrote Golden Girls, she named Bea Arthur's

217
00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:43.200
character Dorothy Zabornak.

218
00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:44.780
Amazing!

219
00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:45.820
Yes!

220
00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.420
He was the inspiration behind that name.

221
00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:52.180
He told me he was beyond excited by this honor.

222
00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.080
He was like, I mean, who wouldn't be?

223
00:10:54.300 --> 00:11:00.060
And then he went on to be the first assistant director on Golden Girls, and he said Bea Arthur

224
00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.700
was like a second mother to him.

225
00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:02.800
He just loved her.

226
00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.040
That is so wonderful.

227
00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.440
I love all of that.

228
00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:07.580
We love you, Kent.

229
00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.600
Okay, rounding out my fast facts.

230
00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.000
Fast fact number three.

231
00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.280
Angela, you came up with this idea, and I just loved it.

232
00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.900
I think we should do it for every character.

233
00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.900
And now I'm like, oh, we might have missed a few.

234
00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:25.220
We might have to, in a revisited, do this for other characters.

235
00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.300
That's right.

236
00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:27.940
Here's what we're talking about.

237
00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:33.320
Angela said, whenever we say goodbye to a character, we should give them a show Bible

238
00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:33.720
goodbye.

239
00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:39.800
So I went through the show Bible, and I gathered facts about Toby Flunderson.

240
00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:40.440
Yay!

241
00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.400
Here they are.

242
00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:48.060
Toby Flunderson, graduate of Bishop O'Hara High School, class of 89.

243
00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:54.880
He is divorced, but his wife is still his emergency contact, although her last name is Becker

244
00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:55.160
now.

245
00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.200
Hmm.

246
00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:02.540
During his 12 years working HR at Dunder Mifflin, he has explained female anatomy to Dwight,

247
00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:07.920
told Kevin he should ditch Dunder Mifflin's health care plan and get on his fiancee Stacy's

248
00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:10.380
plan instead because it's definitely going to be better.

249
00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:17.100
He sent out a memo regarding Jim and Pam's PDA, and he attended Jan's deposition and was

250
00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.000
present for the reading of Michael's diary.

251
00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.380
Toby is one of the founding members of the Finer Things Club.

252
00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:27.940
He bought Angela her baby jazz poster, and he can run a mile in seven minutes.

253
00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:33.200
He's been trying to flirt with Pam and ask her out ever since season three.

254
00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.940
That is also how long he's been talking about going to Costa Rica.

255
00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:41.340
He started talking about that ever since he heard the Scranton branch might be closing.

256
00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:46.920
And now, after a very awkward moment of rubbing Pam's knee, he is finally leaving.

257
00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:50.160
Although, guys, he is going to come back.

258
00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:50.920
Spoiler alert.

259
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.140
Oh, I love that.

260
00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.900
I love the show Bible goodbye.

261
00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:55.540
Show Bible goodbye.

262
00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.280
It's like a show Bible eulogy.

263
00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:58.160
Mm-hmm.

264
00:12:58.360 --> 00:12:58.880
A little bit.

265
00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:03.160
Well, we'll definitely have to do that for a few characters in a Revisited, like for

266
00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:03.980
Karen Filippelli.

267
00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.900
Oh, yeah.

268
00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.360
That's got to be in a Revisited.

269
00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:08.400
We'll do it.

270
00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.000
That is all I have, Angela.

271
00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.800
Quick fast facts today.

272
00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:12.920
I like it.

273
00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.420
I have some fun stuff from the shooting draft.

274
00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:18.760
But maybe before we get into this episode, we should take a little break.

275
00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.740
Let's take a little break, but I've got a lot to say about this one.

276
00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:25.600
So, we might be short here up on top, but we're going to be long later.

277
00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.620
That's what she said?

278
00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.000
Is that a thing she said?

279
00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:30.820
Maybe.

280
00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:31.600
Maybe.

281
00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:32.520
I don't know.

282
00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.220
You decide over the break.

283
00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:34.780
Okay.

284
00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:45.770
All right.

285
00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:46.730
We are back.

286
00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.790
And Michael is so excited to have his moment.

287
00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:52.670
It is time for Toby's exit interview.

288
00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:54.850
Michael shows up with a gift.

289
00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.330
It's wrapped.

290
00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:57.230
There's a ribbon.

291
00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:58.010
Yeah.

292
00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.650
He walks in the conference room with Toby.

293
00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:00.570
He shuts the door.

294
00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.330
He's ready to get started.

295
00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.650
But then what happens?

296
00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.130
He says this.

297
00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:12.310
Can I just say that of all the idiots and all the idiot villages and all the idiot worlds,

298
00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.510
you stand alone, my friend.

299
00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:20.990
And then right as he's about to really go off, Holly enters.

300
00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:22.890
And he's like, oh, hey.

301
00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.330
And she's like, yeah, I've got to be here.

302
00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:27.150
This is part of my job.

303
00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:27.930
And he's like, no, no, no.

304
00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.170
Shouldn't you just tour some more?

305
00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.070
Go see the Baylor.

306
00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.650
She goes, maybe later.

307
00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:33.250
This is actually part of my job.

308
00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:34.470
And then Pam walks in.

309
00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.170
She's like, do you need me to take notes?

310
00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:37.690
Toby's all over it.

311
00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:38.410
Toby's like, stay.

312
00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:39.170
Pam, stay.

313
00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:40.290
She's like, all right.

314
00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.390
Well, this is now not going as Michael had planned.

315
00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:45.110
He gets out his note cards.

316
00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:48.350
He's written some questions.

317
00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.650
Again, Steve Carell should have won 15 Emmys.

318
00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:52.530
I mean, come on.

319
00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:52.950
Yeah.

320
00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:59.630
This is his having all this stuff he wanted to just tee off on Toby about and now having

321
00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:04.690
to dial it back and somehow be acceptable in front of this woman he's falling in love with.

322
00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.950
Every moment, Steve crushes.

323
00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:12.430
His first question is, who do you think you are?

324
00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.290
And Toby goes, I'm Toby.

325
00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:21.950
Now, I hope you noticed in the background, I'm going to toot my own horn.

326
00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.690
I am taking notes.

327
00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:24.670
No, I know.

328
00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:26.910
I watched you write it all down.

329
00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:31.090
And I am actually writing down, who are you?

330
00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:32.870
And then I wrote down Toby.

331
00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:36.510
And a couple times I wrote down, he is Toby.

332
00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.890
But my whole backstory, and Angela, I loved doing these scenes.

333
00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:45.770
I loved every time Pam's sole purpose in a scene was to take notes.

334
00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:47.490
Because I was just an audience member.

335
00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.730
I got to just sit there.

336
00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.770
I didn't have any like real lines I had to say or anything I had to do.

337
00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:53.910
You just had to try not to laugh.

338
00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:54.770
Pretty much.

339
00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.330
But I always took diligent notes.

340
00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:58.630
I really did.

341
00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:04.130
Because I liked to pretend that Michael would ask me to transcribe these meetings later.

342
00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:08.170
I like to think he made you go in his office and read the whole thing back to him.

343
00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:09.910
Just so he could feel important.

344
00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:15.050
This was like something he saw in an old movie once that secretaries do for their bosses.

345
00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:15.910
That's right.

346
00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:19.630
His second note card says, what gives you the right?

347
00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:23.510
And this is when Holly steps in.

348
00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:24.230
She's like, you know what?

349
00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.030
I brought the binder.

350
00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:26.770
Do you want to use it?

351
00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:27.730
Take a look at it?

352
00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:28.450
Yeah.

353
00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:34.750
And Michael starts to ask Toby if he has any suggestions on ways that, you know, Dunder Mifflin

354
00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:35.670
could improve itself.

355
00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:42.950
And Toby seems like he's going to answer this question until, oh my God, Steve puts his hands

356
00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:46.210
up to his face to shield himself from Holly.

357
00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.830
And he gives Toby this look.

358
00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:49.850
It's so good.

359
00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:53.350
He actually mouths the words, I'll kill you.

360
00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:57.430
I missed it.

361
00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.370
He says, I'll kill you.

362
00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:05.230
And in the script, it's written that he does the slit the throat, you know, the finger across

363
00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.210
the throat gesture.

364
00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:06.710
Yeah.

365
00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:09.270
But I don't know if this was Steve improvising.

366
00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:11.630
I feel like he probably gave them a few different choices.

367
00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.570
But the one they picked was him whispering.

368
00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:18.540
It's so amazing.

369
00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:22.040
And Toby just goes, I guess everything's okay.

370
00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:23.100
Yeah.

371
00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.740
And he's like, you know, he has this moment where he's like, I mean, I made it this far.

372
00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:28.440
Why not?

373
00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:31.400
Well, Pam is going to suggest that Toby open his gift.

374
00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:32.500
Toby, open it.

375
00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:33.320
What is it?

376
00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:34.760
And Michael's like, no, no, no, no, no.

377
00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:35.280
You know what?

378
00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:43.300
You guys, it's a rock with a note on it that says, suck on this.

379
00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.360
I watched this episode with Lee.

380
00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:49.240
Lee, he laughed so hard at this joke.

381
00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.420
He couldn't stop laughing that it was a rock.

382
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.160
He just thought that was so funny.

383
00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.300
Michael, you know, acts like he had no idea.

384
00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:01.040
And he's like, who pulled this prank on Toby?

385
00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:01.800
This is horrible.

386
00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.520
And Dwight's like, you told me to do it.

387
00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:04.120
And he's like, shh.

388
00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:05.440
And then he goes, you know what this was?

389
00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.880
It was a psych, psych, psyched you out because there's a real gift coming.

390
00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:16.640
And this is my second favorite thing to do as Pam after taking notes in a meeting, which

391
00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.880
is painting Michael into a corner.

392
00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:22.200
And she says, what's the gift, Michael?

393
00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.520
What is it?

394
00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.000
Oh, is it your watch?

395
00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:29.000
And he's like, it is.

396
00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.000
It is my watch.

397
00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:30.760
How did you know?

398
00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.520
And she says, I just knew.

399
00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:34.300
He's so ticked off.

400
00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.480
He has to give Toby his watch.

401
00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:37.340
You know what?

402
00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.460
That's a genuine Seiko piece.

403
00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.280
He's going to have to give Toby the certificate that's framed as well, I guess.

404
00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.380
I guess he will.

405
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.440
This delightful scene is interrupted by some hubbub in the bullpen.

406
00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:53.960
Everyone is gathered around Jim's computer watching a YouTube video.

407
00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:54.880
Yeah.

408
00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:56.740
Ryan is being arrested.

409
00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.140
And someone has uploaded the moment.

410
00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:00.980
And they're all watching it.

411
00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:05.800
I want you guys to know that they actually put that video on YouTube.

412
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.160
It was a private account.

413
00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:11.500
So John is actually watching it during that scene.

414
00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:12.340
We all are.

415
00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:13.940
But it was a private account.

416
00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:19.720
When the episode aired, they made the video go live on YouTube so everyone could watch it.

417
00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:20.960
Oh, that's so great.

418
00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:22.100
I didn't know that.

419
00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:22.620
Yeah.

420
00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.400
But Michael is very upset.

421
00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:27.000
He's in his office.

422
00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:30.420
And Holly is saying to Toby, what do you do in this situation?

423
00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.100
Toby says, I don't do anything.

424
00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.400
Just leave it alone.

425
00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:35.480
But Holly is amazing.

426
00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.860
She goes into Michael's office and she really comforts him.

427
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:39.860
Michael is crying.

428
00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.140
He's really sweet.

429
00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:43.020
He says, I'm worried about my friend.

430
00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:43.780
Yeah.

431
00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.200
And she says, that's normal.

432
00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.900
You take the time you need to have your feelings.

433
00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.800
Which leads to just a wonderful talking head, Angela, that I love.

434
00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:57.260
Where Michael says, Holly is sweet and simple like a lady baker.

435
00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:03.040
And he just wouldn't be surprised to find out that she'd worked in a bakery before coming to Dunder Mifflin.

436
00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:06.380
I mean, he's pretty sure she's baked on a professional level.

437
00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:08.760
Because baking is love, right?

438
00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:09.420
Yeah.

439
00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:11.180
Only sweet ladies bake.

440
00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.100
Sweet ladies who take care of you.

441
00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:13.820
Yeah.

442
00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:14.720
Aw.

443
00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:22.140
Well, after this very sweet Michael talking head, we are all going to go out in the parking lot because the party is starting.

444
00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:23.080
Oh, yeah.

445
00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:27.940
But before we get into that parking lot, Jenna, I need to share a little back story.

446
00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:29.140
Okay.

447
00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:37.360
Have you ever been on the phone with someone and you actually hear that person go into a full flop sweat?

448
00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.180
Where is this going?

449
00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.080
Because I have.

450
00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:41.880
Okay.

451
00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:42.920
I have.

452
00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.820
And that person was Kent Zabornak.

453
00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:45.760
Oh, my gosh.

454
00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:46.820
Oh, gosh.

455
00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:51.720
Not only did I remember this, but then I found some emails between Kent and I that really painted the picture.

456
00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:56.220
And I wanted to share the story with you guys that I almost didn't make it to the parking lot.

457
00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.180
Oh, now I know what you're talking about.

458
00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:07.500
In my emails, I found that on Thursday, April 10th of 2008, at 4 p.m., I had a routine checkup with my OBGYN.

459
00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.020
I emailed Kent about it.

460
00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.540
He said, no problem, Ange.

461
00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:13.560
We'll have you wrapped in time to make it to that doctor's appointment.

462
00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:19.740
So, lady, while I was at my doctor's appointment, you know, how they sort of check all your vitals and do everything.

463
00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:26.520
And I had had, like, I was feeling like a little bit of cramping, but nothing I was really worried about.

464
00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:30.060
And she was like, Angela, you're having contractions.

465
00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.300
And I said, what?

466
00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:32.620
And she said, yeah.

467
00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:35.580
And she immediately sent me to the hospital.

468
00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:37.140
From your doctor's appointment.

469
00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.420
From my doctor's appointment at 4 o'clock.

470
00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:40.520
Now I'm in the hospital.

471
00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.340
I'm having contractions every five minutes.

472
00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:51.400
And around 6 o'clock in the evening, Jenny O'Keefe, who was our second AD, called me to tell me my call time.

473
00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:51.880
Right?

474
00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:53.180
For the next day.

475
00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:53.880
For the next day.

476
00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:54.780
She's like, hi, Angela.

477
00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:56.680
Your call time tomorrow is 5.30 a.m.

478
00:21:56.740 --> 00:21:58.320
And I said, Jenny, I'm in the hospital.

479
00:21:59.020 --> 00:21:59.960
She said, what?

480
00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:02.420
And I said, I'm having contractions.

481
00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:03.260
And she goes, okay.

482
00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:03.920
Okay.

483
00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:06.980
I will get back to you.

484
00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:11.540
Literally three seconds later, my phone rings and it's Kent Sabornak.

485
00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:15.460
And I will never forget the first thing he said to me.

486
00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:17.980
He said, hey, hey, Ange.

487
00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:19.920
Uh, we having this baby today?

488
00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:23.000
But like his voice cracked and went up.

489
00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:24.860
It's like, we having this baby today?

490
00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:30.080
Because what you guys have to know is they were building a freaking Ferris wheel in the parking lot.

491
00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:31.080
That's right.

492
00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:36.920
And to give you guys some context, this was all happening about three weeks before your due date.

493
00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:37.400
Right?

494
00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:37.760
Yeah.

495
00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:40.480
We just had a few more days of filming with you.

496
00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:47.820
Everyone just assumed that we would finish this episode and then you would go off on your summer hiatus and have your baby.

497
00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:50.220
Kent thought he had time.

498
00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:58.360
But in reality, you are in the hospital and he was probably standing in the parking lot as they're assembling this Ferris wheel and he's freaking out.

499
00:22:58.880 --> 00:22:59.240
Yeah.

500
00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:02.700
How does Andy propose if Angela can't be there?

501
00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:03.280
Yeah.

502
00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.320
In front of the Ferris wheel.

503
00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:07.560
So I said, Kent, I don't know.

504
00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:09.120
I don't know if I'm having this baby tonight.

505
00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:11.600
And he said, well, would you keep me posted?

506
00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:13.020
And I said, sure.

507
00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:15.840
And it turned out to be false labor.

508
00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:17.620
I was there till about two in the morning.

509
00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:20.180
I did have to go work a half day the next day.

510
00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:24.560
And let me tell you, Kent had already hired a stunt woman.

511
00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:26.200
Her name was Melissa Barker.

512
00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:29.840
And she was to be my body double for the rest of this shoot.

513
00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:35.080
They really wanted to try to make sure I did not have to work if I was not in a speaking scene.

514
00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:35.480
Right?

515
00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:36.660
They would use Melissa.

516
00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:41.020
Angela, it was so weird to have her on set because she was dressed just like you.

517
00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:42.780
She had her hair done just like you.

518
00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:45.480
From behind, she seriously looked like you.

519
00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:51.800
So, yes, if there was a scene in the conference room and you were just not speaking, she would be sitting there.

520
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:53.900
And I would forget that she wasn't you.

521
00:23:54.520 --> 00:23:54.880
Mm-hmm.

522
00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:58.100
Well, listen, this all happened on a Thursday night.

523
00:23:58.360 --> 00:24:01.420
By Saturday, Kent sent the whole cast this email.

524
00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:03.000
Saturday, April 12th.

525
00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:06.700
Hey, you guys, our one-liner schedule will be coming out later tomorrow.

526
00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:15.620
Please be advised that we are trying to shoot Miss Angela Kinsey out next week so she can go rest easily for a full week before delivering her little girl.

527
00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:22.440
And to accommodate this, Wednesday through Friday's schedule will be more grueling than normal, especially Friday night's work.

528
00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.420
Think Ferris wheel and fireworks.

529
00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:31.580
We will all take extra precautions to ensure Angela is comfortable and that she remains hydrated every single moment she is here.

530
00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:34.120
So, prepare for the walkie-talkie chatter.

531
00:24:34.460 --> 00:24:36.480
Angela's going 10-1 again.

532
00:24:39.540 --> 00:24:42.620
So, yeah, I almost didn't make it to the parking lot.

533
00:24:43.300 --> 00:24:44.680
Well, I'm glad you made it.

534
00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:45.720
I am, too.

535
00:24:46.540 --> 00:24:49.760
I do remember the whole cast and crew were a little worried.

536
00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:50.460
We were concerned.

537
00:24:50.460 --> 00:24:53.820
We wanted to make sure that we got your work done firSt.

538
00:24:54.420 --> 00:24:55.520
So, that you could leave.

539
00:24:55.780 --> 00:24:56.040
Yes.

540
00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:58.040
And I left and Melissa Barker stayed.

541
00:24:58.280 --> 00:24:59.700
So, thank you, Melissa Barker.

542
00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:05.080
And, lady, now everyone is exiting the building, going into the parking lot.

543
00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:07.600
25 minutes, 52 seconds.

544
00:25:07.960 --> 00:25:08.720
Ugg alert.

545
00:25:09.400 --> 00:25:10.880
Who has the Uggs?

546
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:13.840
Who has the warm, fuzzy Uggs on?

547
00:25:13.960 --> 00:25:15.080
Who is this person?

548
00:25:15.440 --> 00:25:16.340
It is me.

549
00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:22.040
And this starts a theme for this episode where they just gave up with me.

550
00:25:22.220 --> 00:25:23.880
They were like, just keep her comfortable.

551
00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:30.200
And I feel like in almost every shot, you can see my belly and I'm wearing Uggs and no one cares.

552
00:25:30.580 --> 00:25:31.240
You know what?

553
00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:35.660
I remember watching Seinfeld when Julia Louis-Dreyfus was pregnant.

554
00:25:35.720 --> 00:25:39.200
And there were a few times where I feel like it was the same.

555
00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:40.520
They were like, you know what?

556
00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:42.040
We all know she's pregnant.

557
00:25:42.240 --> 00:25:45.220
We're pretending like she's not pregnant because her character's not pregnant.

558
00:25:45.460 --> 00:25:48.020
Let's just, we're all in it together, folks.

559
00:25:48.020 --> 00:25:48.580
Yeah.

560
00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:49.920
We're just giving up.

561
00:25:50.620 --> 00:25:51.100
Exactly.

562
00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:58.640
Well, Michael is very disappointed that there is not an anti-gravity machine, but he is impressed with the Ferris wheel.

563
00:25:59.280 --> 00:26:01.120
Yeah, and there's a bouncy house.

564
00:26:01.260 --> 00:26:07.180
Which, by the way, poor Brian, in the heat, had to jump up and down in over and over.

565
00:26:07.240 --> 00:26:08.800
And it was so hot in there.

566
00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:12.220
And there's deleted scenes of him jumping and jumping.

567
00:26:12.400 --> 00:26:14.480
And it didn't even make it in the episode.

568
00:26:14.800 --> 00:26:15.620
I know.

569
00:26:16.160 --> 00:26:23.800
This is also when Pam clocks the fireworks and she realizes, oh my gosh, is Jim going to propose tonight?

570
00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:24.980
She's so excited.

571
00:26:25.320 --> 00:26:27.420
Lady, I thought you were so good in this episode.

572
00:26:27.420 --> 00:26:31.500
I thought your performance was so subtle and the emotion was so there.

573
00:26:31.780 --> 00:26:33.860
I just thought it was a beautiful, beautiful job.

574
00:26:34.120 --> 00:26:34.700
Oh my gosh.

575
00:26:34.840 --> 00:26:35.820
Thank you so much.

576
00:26:36.020 --> 00:26:36.340
Yeah.

577
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:38.980
We had a fan question from Sophie F.

578
00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:42.460
Did you get to go on the rides while you weren't filming?

579
00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:43.680
No.

580
00:26:43.880 --> 00:26:52.740
For insurance purposes, they were not going to let cast members who were not scripted to be on the Ferris wheel get on the Ferris wheel.

581
00:26:53.340 --> 00:26:55.340
They wanted me nowhere near that thing.

582
00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:58.260
They were like, hey, big pregnant lady, you're already freaking us out.

583
00:26:58.520 --> 00:26:59.120
Stay away.

584
00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:01.780
I remember talking to Jen Salata about it.

585
00:27:01.880 --> 00:27:05.100
And she said, oh my gosh, all the riders were like so excited.

586
00:27:05.240 --> 00:27:07.060
They're like, we're going to ride the Ferris wheel.

587
00:27:07.220 --> 00:27:08.240
It's going to be so fun.

588
00:27:08.520 --> 00:27:10.500
And then none of them ever rode it.

589
00:27:10.840 --> 00:27:11.200
No.

590
00:27:11.200 --> 00:27:13.180
I remember when they had the bouncy houses.

591
00:27:13.380 --> 00:27:17.440
Whenever we had a bouncy house, you know, there'd be someone be like, oh, could the kids come by today?

592
00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:18.100
They're like, nope.

593
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.420
No one get on those things.

594
00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:23.400
Well, two people who were allowed to get on the Ferris wheel.

595
00:27:23.720 --> 00:27:26.520
I remember when they shot this, Angela, these poor guys.

596
00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:28.800
Do you know how many times they had to go around that Ferris wheel?

597
00:27:29.040 --> 00:27:34.440
Just as a person who rode the Jurassic Park ride for 12 hours, you know how old it gets.

598
00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:36.160
It's a trigger for you.

599
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:36.560
It is.

600
00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:37.000
It's a trigger.

601
00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:39.980
And I watched them ride that Ferris wheel for about an hour.

602
00:27:40.180 --> 00:27:42.600
I don't understand how they weren't completely sick.

603
00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:47.900
When you watch the episode, you see one scene between Michael and Holly on the Ferris wheel, but there are more.

604
00:27:48.080 --> 00:27:50.680
And they're in the deleted scenes, and they're really cute.

605
00:27:50.680 --> 00:27:52.340
So they were in there for a while.

606
00:27:52.740 --> 00:27:54.000
Yeah, I remember that.

607
00:27:54.400 --> 00:27:59.060
One of the Ferris wheel scenes that I love is Michael is telling Holly a story.

608
00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:03.840
And right as they get to the top of the Ferris wheel, she shakes the cart, like kind of leans forward.

609
00:28:03.840 --> 00:28:04.580
So it rocks.

610
00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:06.060
And he goes, oh, my God.

611
00:28:06.340 --> 00:28:08.020
And then they both start laughing.

612
00:28:08.020 --> 00:28:09.180
And he's like, you got me.

613
00:28:09.300 --> 00:28:11.040
You know, it's so cute.

614
00:28:11.300 --> 00:28:12.960
It's like something Michael would have done.

615
00:28:13.200 --> 00:28:13.460
Yes.

616
00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:16.060
That probably would annoy anyone else.

617
00:28:16.280 --> 00:28:16.660
Yeah.

618
00:28:16.900 --> 00:28:18.540
Because that's an annoying thing to do.

619
00:28:18.740 --> 00:28:19.440
It really is.

620
00:28:19.780 --> 00:28:20.080
Yeah.

621
00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:22.220
And he's delighted by it.

622
00:28:22.540 --> 00:28:23.220
So cute.

623
00:28:23.520 --> 00:28:30.760
Well, when they finally get off the Ferris wheel, Holly catches Mose, Dwight, and Meredith doing something to her car.

624
00:28:30.880 --> 00:28:31.940
What are you doing to my car?

625
00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:36.600
Well, what they're doing is putting a raccoon inside of it because they're still hazing her.

626
00:28:37.380 --> 00:28:37.700
Yeah.

627
00:28:38.180 --> 00:28:43.460
And you guys might be curious, why is Meredith involved with Dwight and Moses hazing?

628
00:28:43.720 --> 00:28:47.900
We learn in a deleted scene that Meredith is not a fan of Holly.

629
00:28:48.320 --> 00:28:49.420
Can you guys play the clip?

630
00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:51.520
I think that makes us neighbors.

631
00:28:51.800 --> 00:28:52.720
It's a couple streets over.

632
00:28:53.160 --> 00:28:57.220
Oh, maybe you can show me some of the fun hangouts or where to get my nails done.

633
00:28:57.320 --> 00:28:57.560
Sure.

634
00:28:57.560 --> 00:28:58.640
That sounds fun.

635
00:28:58.960 --> 00:28:59.400
Great.

636
00:29:00.620 --> 00:29:01.780
I hate that bitch.

637
00:29:02.220 --> 00:29:03.540
I want to cut her face.

638
00:29:03.800 --> 00:29:06.170
It's out of nowhere.

639
00:29:06.630 --> 00:29:08.390
Holly is like, hey, I think we're neighbors.

640
00:29:08.570 --> 00:29:09.810
Maybe we could do stuff together.

641
00:29:10.010 --> 00:29:13.930
And then immediately as she walks away, Meredith is like, I hate that bitch.

642
00:29:14.190 --> 00:29:16.090
And Dwight overhears this.

643
00:29:16.230 --> 00:29:17.150
And he's like, uh-huh.

644
00:29:17.590 --> 00:29:18.990
I have an accomplice.

645
00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:23.870
And there's all these really fun scenes between Dwight and Meredith as they plan out all these

646
00:29:23.870 --> 00:29:24.730
different pranks.

647
00:29:24.970 --> 00:29:25.550
They're great.

648
00:29:25.730 --> 00:29:26.570
They're on the DVD.

649
00:29:26.930 --> 00:29:32.170
And I texted with Kate because in the script, there's some direction I want to read to you.

650
00:29:32.290 --> 00:29:34.430
It says, Michael leads Holly away.

651
00:29:34.650 --> 00:29:40.430
In the background, Dwight casually opens Holly's car door, releasing the badger.

652
00:29:40.910 --> 00:29:42.230
Then there's an asterisk.

653
00:29:42.450 --> 00:29:45.710
And it says the raccoon instantly attacks Meredith.

654
00:29:45.710 --> 00:29:48.350
So I was like, is it a badger or is it a raccoon?

655
00:29:48.490 --> 00:29:53.730
But either way, I texted Kate and I said, did you have to film getting attacked by a raccoon?

656
00:29:54.290 --> 00:30:00.170
Jen Salata said the original outline for the script had them putting a badger in the car

657
00:30:00.170 --> 00:30:02.630
instead of a raccoon.

658
00:30:02.750 --> 00:30:07.930
But they couldn't find a trained badger to attack Meredith.

659
00:30:08.470 --> 00:30:09.230
Well, who knew?

660
00:30:09.590 --> 00:30:13.970
So Kent got a raccoon from this place called Critters of the Cinema.

661
00:30:13.970 --> 00:30:22.370
But then they realized that even a raccoon is not really trained well enough for an attack

662
00:30:22.370 --> 00:30:27.950
scene, at least not to the point where they felt like they wanted Kate to have a raccoon

663
00:30:27.950 --> 00:30:28.370
on her.

664
00:30:28.710 --> 00:30:28.890
Yeah.

665
00:30:29.030 --> 00:30:31.810
So they hired a stunt double to do it.

666
00:30:31.830 --> 00:30:36.070
But then they realized the best way to do it was maybe with CGI.

667
00:30:36.070 --> 00:30:44.570
So they did a shot of Kate just flailing around as if she was being attacked by a raccoon.

668
00:30:44.730 --> 00:30:47.230
But in the end, the whole thing got cut.

669
00:30:47.690 --> 00:30:47.830
Yeah.

670
00:30:48.230 --> 00:30:54.430
However, Kate said that there is a scene later where she has scratch marks on her face.

671
00:30:54.790 --> 00:30:54.930
Yeah.

672
00:30:55.110 --> 00:30:59.230
I texted Kate and she said they filmed her screaming and running around.

673
00:30:59.270 --> 00:31:01.490
Then they didn't end up using any of it.

674
00:31:01.490 --> 00:31:05.630
And she said, once again, the animals have better representation than me.

675
00:31:06.770 --> 00:31:07.890
That's very funny.

676
00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:11.050
Because she always gets roped into these animal attacks.

677
00:31:11.530 --> 00:31:17.050
I found an old interview that Mike Schur did as Moe's talking about the raccoon.

678
00:31:17.350 --> 00:31:18.030
Oh, yeah?

679
00:31:18.250 --> 00:31:20.550
This is what Moe's has to say about it.

680
00:31:20.810 --> 00:31:23.230
Quote, I love the raccoon.

681
00:31:23.410 --> 00:31:28.010
The raccoon's name is Chair because when I found him, he was eating a chair.

682
00:31:28.630 --> 00:31:31.610
He has a brother named Trampoline Legg.

683
00:31:31.650 --> 00:31:32.930
Chair is very nice.

684
00:31:33.170 --> 00:31:35.030
I made sure Chair got home safely.

685
00:31:35.310 --> 00:31:39.950
Chair would never hurt anyone except once Chair bit my cheek when I was feeding him a lemon.

686
00:31:40.610 --> 00:31:40.990
End quote.

687
00:31:41.550 --> 00:31:43.230
Moe's the conversationaliSt.

688
00:31:43.710 --> 00:31:46.630
Michael really comes to Holly's defense, you know?

689
00:31:46.950 --> 00:31:53.910
He tells them they should be ashamed of themselves and that Holly is the best thing to happen to this company since World War II.

690
00:31:53.910 --> 00:32:00.250
And she is going to be so appreciative that she touches Michael's arm and it kind of lingers there for a second.

691
00:32:00.490 --> 00:32:01.470
For a second?

692
00:32:01.470 --> 00:32:02.250
I counted.

693
00:32:02.730 --> 00:32:04.030
Nine seconds.

694
00:32:04.430 --> 00:32:05.170
Count that out.

695
00:32:05.510 --> 00:32:17.170
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine.

696
00:32:17.610 --> 00:32:18.570
Come on.

697
00:32:18.730 --> 00:32:20.570
That's a lingering touch right there.

698
00:32:21.110 --> 00:32:23.130
This talking head broke my heart.

699
00:32:23.890 --> 00:32:24.370
Oh.

700
00:32:25.570 --> 00:32:26.730
He's so excited.

701
00:32:27.130 --> 00:32:28.670
This is so good.

702
00:32:28.930 --> 00:32:30.970
He says, did you see that?

703
00:32:31.150 --> 00:32:31.970
Did you see that?

704
00:32:32.250 --> 00:32:34.650
He's kind of talking to the documentarian crew, right?

705
00:32:34.810 --> 00:32:37.390
He's like, you know, Jan didn't believe in affection.

706
00:32:37.390 --> 00:32:42.090
So sometimes he just doesn't know how to react when a girl touches him, but he really likes it.

707
00:32:43.050 --> 00:32:43.390
Oh.

708
00:32:43.650 --> 00:32:45.550
Holly is so perfect for him.

709
00:32:45.790 --> 00:32:46.470
I know.

710
00:32:46.910 --> 00:32:49.050
But there's a problem at the party, Angela.

711
00:32:49.250 --> 00:32:51.850
I'm sorry to tell you, the barbecue sauce is out.

712
00:32:52.290 --> 00:32:52.930
Oh, yeah.

713
00:32:53.470 --> 00:32:55.910
By the way, do you know who's doing the barbecuing?

